(2) If a limited partner, other than a trust corporation acting in such capacity for the purposes of this Order, takes part in the conduct of the business of the ILP with persons who are not partners, then, subject to subsection (3), in the event of the insolvency of the ILP, the limited partner shall be liable, as though he were a general partner, for all debts and obligations of the ILP incurred during the period that he does so take part.

(3) When a limited partner becomes liable by virtue of subsection (2), he shall be so liable only in respect of a debt or obligation incurred by the ILP in favour of a person who, at the time the debt or obligation was incurred, reasonably on the basis of the conduct of the limited partner, that the limited partner was a general partner; and the assignment or other transfer of any such debt or obligation at any time before the insolvency of the ILP shall not affect any liability under subsection (2).

